{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3873","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3873","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3873\",\"parent_revision\":\"479d8756ca869b0278d34f91733378e0c583adaa153e896d33786de719b4c404\",\"root_revision\":\"479d8756ca869b0278d34f91733378e0c583adaa153e896d33786de719b4c404\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Desired outcome\\n\\nA JSON-only `backend status [optional-reference]` capability must expose CLI-owned configuration and routing context plus the selected adapter's own `status()` result. With a reference it reports that reference's routed adapter; without one it reports the configured primary adapter. Every adapter result has stable `availability` and extensible adapter-owned `details`. Online adapters probe availability and authentication by default within one 30-second overall timeout. Reachable exits successfully; timeout, authentication, rate-limit, and other connection errors exit nonzero and remain structured. No result exposes secrets, raw environment values, or unsafe exception text.\\n\\nSQLite may report its database path and counts. GitHub may report authentication state, username, and offline-cache state. Adapter-specific status remains under `details`; the initial common schema stays minimal.\\n\\n## Observed gap and evidence\\n\\nCurrent code exposes `probe_backend_status()` and the current `BackendStatus` shape. The preflight found no JSON-only, reference-aware command or common adapter-owned `availability`/`details` envelope. Closed #1015 and #3599 cover earlier adjacent status behavior only.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nAn operator cannot confirm which backend a Work Brief reference will use or distinguish reachability, authentication, timeout, and other provider-owned conditions before work begins.\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns diagnostics, not routing policy. It adds no speculative common fields beyond `availability` and `details`, and does not flatten provider connection errors.\\n\\n## Readiness and acceptance conditions\\n\\nStatus always emits valid JSON. Reference and no-reference calls report the correct selected adapter. Online probes are bounded to 30 seconds, all required non-reachable outcomes are structured and nonzero, adapter details are meaningful to that backend, and sensitive values are absent.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn operator cannot confirm which backend a Work Brief reference will use or distinguish reachability, authentication, timeout, and other provider-owned conditions before work begins.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User-confirmed Work Brief grilling session; 2026-09-24 backend-status evidence\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA JSON-only `backend status [optional-reference]` capability must expose CLI-owned configuration and routing context plus the selected adapter's own `status()` result. With a reference it reports that reference's routed adapter; without one it reports the configured primary adapter. Every adapter result has stable `availability` and extensible adapter-owned `details`. Online adapters probe availability and authentication by default within one 30-second overall timeout. Reachable exits successfully; timeout, authentication, rate-limit, and other connection errors exit nonzero and remain structured. No result exposes secrets, raw environment values, or unsafe exception text.\\n\\nSQLite may report its database path and counts. GitHub may report authentication state, username, and offline-cache state. Adapter-specific status remains under `details`; the initial common schema stays minimal.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Readiness And Acceptance Conditions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nStatus always emits valid JSON. Reference and no-reference calls report the correct selected adapter. Online probes are bounded to 30 seconds, all required non-reachable outcomes are structured and nonzero, adapter details are meaningful to that backend, and sensitive values are absent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Boundaries\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns diagnostics, not routing policy. It adds no speculative common fields beyond `availability` and `details`, and does not flatten provider connection errors.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Gap And Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCurrent code exposes `probe_backend_status()` and the current `BackendStatus` shape. The preflight found no JSON-only, reference-aware command or common adapter-owned `availability`/`details` envelope. Closed #1015 and #3599 cover earlier adjacent status behavior only.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ddbf970126a6ea672a5aafa5e5498ce2596ae420f8b2dea843395b5825b07dee\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWnrzww\"}"}